/*
:name: concat_two_lanes
:type: compile
*/

// `concat(a, b)` — the call-shaped bit-concatenation builtin. No grammar was
// added for it: prp2lnast recognizes the callee and emits the n-ary LNAST
// `concat` node (argument 0 = the MOST significant lane, Verilog `{a,b}`
// order), and upass.tolg turns that into one Ntype_op::Concat whose per-lane
// window comes from each lane's DECLARED type — never from the live value.
//
// `:type: compile` runs the whole flow: upass.tolg builds the cell (so the
// windows really come from `a:u4` / `b:u2` -- a `:type: upass` run would stop
// before the only pass that reads the declared widths) and inou.cgen.verilog
// then emits it as `{a, b}`.
//
// z is u6 = 4 + 2 (the lane sum), with `a` occupying bits [5..2]; the result of
// a concat is always non-negative, hence unsigned.
comb concat_two_lanes(a:u4, b:u2) -> (z:u6) {
  z = (b, a)#[..]
}
